    "title": "APRIL 20 | Birthdays and Events",
    "text": "Notable Birthdays for April 20William Bartram (1739-1823) - The first first naturalist to document the tropical forests of Florida.Daniel Chester French (1850-1931) - Sculptor who designed the Lincoln statue. Charles Gordon Curtis (1860-1953) - Inventor of the Curtis Steam Turbine, which helped generate electricity on steam boats.George Stibitz (1904-1995) - Considered to be the \"Father of the Modern Digital Computer.\"Betty Lou Gerson (1914-1999) - Voice actress of Cruella de Vil in the Disney 1961 animation 101 Dalmatians.George Takei (1937-Still Living) - Actor widely recognized for his role as Hikaru Sulu in the Star Trek franchise. Jessica Lange (1949-Still Living) - Multi-award winning actress on the big screen and stage.Crispin Glover (1964-Still Living) - Actor who played the quirky character George McFly in Back to the Future.David Filo (1966-Still Living) - Co-founded Yahoo!Memorable Events for April 201777 - New York adopts new a constitution as an independent state. 1894 - Coal mine workers go on strike in Ohio for a pay increase.1898 - The U.S. Assay Office opens in Deadwood, SD.1940 - The first electron microscope is demonstrated by RCA in Philadelphia, PA.1945 - The U.S. 7th Army captures Nuremberg. 1961 - Harold Graham rises about 4 feet high in the first rocket belt flight.1999 - The Columbine High School shooting occurs.2008 - Danica Patrick becomes the first woman to win the Indy Japan 300 car race. Upcoming Dates",
